<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
    <!--
    Notarization requires the hardened runtime, and Apple documents
    com.apple.security.device.audio-input as required for a hardened process to
    use the microphone.

    What was measured here on 2026-09-05 (macOS 26.6), so nobody re-derives it:
    on a Mac that ALREADY holds a TCC microphone grant for com.am.presstalk, a
    hardened build captures audio with or without this entitlement. 26,400
    frames in every one of five paired runs. So this entitlement is not what
    keeps dictation working on an already-approved machine.

    The case that matters is the one that cannot be tested here: a fresh Mac
    with no prior grant, where the first microphone prompt has to succeed. Every
    existing grant is keyed to the current signing identity, so switching to
    Developer ID puts every user back into exactly that untested state. Ship the
    entitlement.

    Keep this list minimal. PressTalk loads no third-party dylibs, uses no JIT,
    and sends no Apple Events, so it needs no other exception.

    Note for editors: XML forbids a double hyphen inside a comment. plutil
    accepts such a file; AMFI rejects it at signing time with "syntax error".
    -->
    <key>com.apple.security.device.audio-input</key>
    <true/>
</dict>
</plist>
